      "properties": [
        {
          "name": "solidsyslog:scope",
          "value": "Core/ and Platform/ subdirectories, plus root-level CMakeLists.txt, CMakePresets.json, and LICENSE.md (shipped library source + build contract + licence text). Tests/, Bdd/, ci/, docs/, .devcontainer/, .github/, sbom/, scripts/, and the other root-level docs/meta files are out of scope (reference / harness / CI / dev-infra / meta, not shipped product)."
        },
        {
          "name": "solidsyslog:runtime-environment",
          "value": "Core requires a C99 compiler and four standard headers (<stddef.h>, <stdbool.h>, <stdint.h>, <string.h>); it calls memcpy and strlen and nothing else from the standard library, and makes no operating-system calls. It requires no operating system, network stack, filesystem or heap. Everything a deployment needs beyond that is supplied by the platform adapters the integrator selects or writes."
        },
        {
          "name": "solidsyslog:platform-backends",
          "value": "Optional, integrator-selected, never vendored. Reference adapters ship for POSIX, Windows, FreeRTOS, lwIP, FreeRTOS-Plus-TCP, ChaN FatFs, FreeRTOS-Plus-FAT, OpenSSL and Mbed TLS; an integrator may instead supply their own for an RTOS or bare-metal target with no shipped pack. Whichever are selected are the integrator's dependencies, with their own versions and licence terms, and belong in the product SBOM rather than this one."
        }
      ]
